    {
     "key": "gja5a",
     "title": "The gja5a fin-length link, withdrawn",
     "body": "Offered as a second tie to the bioelectric fin-size story. It does not hold: the zebrafish fin-length connexin is gja1b, gja5a has no ZFIN fin record, and Daane’s own text puts cx43 under constrained, not accelerated, evolution.",
     "who": "our own cell-to-cell check",
     "where": "genotype/nanopubs/DECISIONS.md"
    },
    {
     "key": "genome",
     "title": "The flying-fish genome claim, wrong",
     "body": "We said almost no molecular data exists for flying fish. An annotated genome does exist, and the error was load-bearing: it was repeated on every number in the map.",
     "who": "the project lead, not the thread that published it",
     "where": "genotype/nanopubs/unsigned/correction-flying-fish-genome-exists.trig"
    },
    {
     "key": "rayinterray",
     "title": "A declared null, withdrawn",
     "body": "We published that no ray-to-interray signalling could be sourced in any fin of any fish. 3 papers contradict it, 1 of them already cited by the same thread on a title-only read. A title-only read was allowed to carry a universal negative; what survives is narrower and none of it pectoral.",
     "who": "our own curation pass, not the thread that wrote it",
     "where": "genotype/nanopubs/unsigned/correction-ray-interray-null-narrowed.trig"
    },
    {
     "key": "lat4a",
     "title": "An overstated “settled”, withdrawn",
     "body": "We said lat4a’s identity was settled on three records. Which gene carries the allele IS resolved to slc43a2a, on the paper’s own chromosome-15 mapping and ZFIN’s allele assignment. Which paralogue carries the flying-fish signal is not: in the paper’s own data both are accelerated, the other more strongly.",
     "who": "a collaborator’s independent cross-check",
     "where": "genotype/map.vetted.json"
    }
   ],
   "variantMismatch": "The zebrafish allele this project's design uses is T200K; the convergent substitution reported in flying fishes is F326L. Different sites, different species, and not the same variant."
